# Hire AI

Hire AI is a full-stack recruitment platform for candidates, recruiters, interviewers, and administrators. It combines relational hiring data with semantic vector matching, applicant relationship graphs, secure resume storage, caching, and audit logging.

## Features

### Candidate

- Register and maintain a role profile.
- Optionally provide LinkedIn and GitHub as either usernames or full profile URLs.
- Browse active jobs with paginated results.
- View job ID, company, salary, qualifications, country, location, skills, and description.
- Upload versioned PDF or DOCX resumes.
- Securely view uploaded resumes through temporary Azure Blob SAS URLs.
- Apply to jobs with a selected resume.
- View submitted applications.
- Receive semantic job recommendations.

LinkedIn and GitHub inputs are validated against their official domains and stored as canonical URLs. If either field is omitted during registration, resume parsing looks for full profile links or labeled usernames such as `LinkedIn: jane-doe` and `GitHub username: @janedoe`. Parsed values only fill missing fields and never overwrite a profile supplied by the candidate.

### Recruiter / HR

- Register using a company verification code.
- Create, update, publish, and close jobs.
- Download a bulk-applicant CSV template per job.
- Upload up to 200 applicants and their resumes in one batch.
- View applicants ranked by semantic resume/job similarity.
- Click an applicant name to open the Neo4j relationship graph.
- Review matched skills, missing skills, semantic score, and suitability explanation.
- Schedule interviews.

### Interviewer

- Register against a verified company.
- View assigned interviews.
- Submit interview feedback and scores.

### Administrator

- Use the configured administrator login.
- View role-specific profile information.
- Manage companies, users, jobs, candidates, recruiters, interviewers, applications, and resumes.
- Use stable public IDs such as `COMP_001`, `USER_001`, `JOB_001`, and `CAND_001` without replacing database keys.
- Search, filter, sort, and paginate all major datasets server-side.
- Securely view, download, and delete eligible resumes.
- Review protected company verification codes.

Configure initial administrator credentials through environment variables before first startup:

```dotenv
DEFAULT_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
DEFAULT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-unique-password
```

## Architecture

```text
Browser
  |
  v
React + Vite / Nginx
  |
  v
FastAPI REST API
  |
  +-- PostgreSQL       users, companies, jobs, applications, profiles
  +-- Azure Blob       PDF/DOCX resume files
  +-- Azure OpenAI     embeddings and match explanations
  +-- Qdrant           resume/job vectors and semantic ranking
  +-- Neo4j            applicant/job/company/resume/skill relationships
  +-- Redis            API response and profile cache
  +-- JSON logs        service logs and central audit trail
```

## Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React, Vite, React Router, Lucide icons, custom CSS |
| Backend | FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLAlchemy |
| Primary database | PostgreSQL |
| Authentication | JWT and Argon2 |
| Resume storage | Azure Blob Storage |
| Embeddings | Azure OpenAI `text-embedding-3-large` |
| Vector database | Qdrant 1.19 |
| Graph database | Neo4j 5 Community |
| Cache | Redis 7.4 |
| Reverse proxy | Nginx |
| Deployment | Docker Compose |
| Tests | Pytest, FastAPI TestClient |

